---
import TopNav from '../../components/TopNav.astro';
import SEO from '../../components/SEO.astro';

const faq = [
	{
		q: "What should I do in 10th grade to prepare for college?",
		a: "Take a free practice SAT and ACT to get a baseline and see which test fits you. Keep your grades up, take on a real leadership role in your main activity, and consider a competition, summer program, or internship in your field."
	},
	{
		q: "What do people get wrong about 10th grade and college prep?",
		a: "Worrying about the PSAT 10 score, which doesn't count toward anything — it's purely practice, and different from the PSAT/NMSQT taken in 11th grade, which is the one that counts toward National Merit."
	},
	{
		q: "Does 10th grade count on a college application?",
		a: "Yes — 10th grade is the first full year of grades colleges really consider, since 9th grade is often treated as a transition period. Course rigor also starts to matter more this year."
	},
	{
		q: "What tests or deadlines matter in 10th grade?",
		a: "PSAT 10 in the spring and AP exams in May, plus a practice SAT and ACT to find a baseline score."
	}
];
const faqSchema = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "FAQPage",
	"mainEntity": faq.map((item) => ({
		"@type": "Question",
		"name": item.q,
		"acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": item.a }
	}))
};
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8" />
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
	<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
	<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
	<SEO
		title="10th Grade College Prep: Go Deeper, Not Wider — Six Years Out"
		description="Take a baseline SAT and ACT, take on real leadership, and keep your grades up — what actually matters in 10th grade."
		path="/grades/10"
	/>
	<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
	<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,600;9..144,700&family=Inter:wght@400;500&display=swap">
</head>
<body>
<TopNav current="grades" />

<article class="grade-page">
  <header class="grade-head">
    <div class="grade-badge">10</div>
    <span class="eyebrow">Grade 10</span>
    <h1>Go deeper, not wider</h1>
    <p class="lede">Continue on with one extracurricular that you're committed to, rather than adding more.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="grade-section">
    <h2>What to do now</h2>
    <p>Take a free practice SAT and ACT now to see which one suits you. Doing this now provides you with the benefits of having a baseline score to go off of, as well as simply helping you to find out which one you should take later, without leaving you guessing.</p>
    <p>Keep your grades up! 10th grade is not the time to be slacking off. Grades from this year are the second most important on your application, after those of 11th grade.</p>
    <p>Take a leadership role in your main activity. Doing one now helps you build vital life skills and strengthens your future college and job applications. You also learn how to communicate clearly, solve problems, and manage your time on a higher stakes scale. Admissions officers are looking for dedication and initiative, not just participation. In 10th grade, you've hopefully been doing this activity for two or more years, meaning you have enough information and experience to guide others.</p>
    <p>10th grade is also not a bad time to consider entering a competition in your field, or to do a summer program or internship. Doing any number of these can provide better recommendations, since you're working closely with mentors and professionals in your field, as well as introducing you to a professional working environment — both of which help you gain credibility and confidence.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grade-section">
    <h2>What most people get wrong</h2>
    <p>10th grade is when you take the PSAT (Preliminary SAT), but it doesn't mean anything on its own. All it is is preparation for the SAT later on, but too many students waste their time worrying about their score when they could be focusing on taking practice tests that actually tell you something.</p>
    <p>Worth knowing: the PSAT 10 is different from the PSAT/NMSQT you'll take in 11th grade. Only the 11th grade version counts toward National Merit — this one is purely practice too.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grade-section">
    <h2>What counts</h2>
    <p>Aside from your first real leadership in something you've already done for a while, your 10th grade year is the first full year of grades colleges really consider. Yes, they see your 9th grade ones as well, but 9th grade is also the period most colleges view as a "transition period," while 10th grade is where your trends and habits truly establish themselves.</p>
    <p>Course rigor also starts to matter more this year. Junior year is when colleges look closest at your schedule, so 10th grade is a reasonable time to start easing into harder classes rather than jumping straight from easy to hardest in one year.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grade-section">
    <h2>Tests and deadlines</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>PSAT 10 in the spring</li>
      <li>AP exams in May</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="related">
    <h2>More resources</h2>
    <div class="related-grid">
      <a class="article-card" href="/study-resources">
        <h3>Resources</h3>
        <p>SAT and ACT prep resources, ranked with an actual opinion.</p>
        <span class="read-more">Read more →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="article-card" href="/summer-programs">
        <h3>Are summer programs and internships worth it?</h3>
        <p>The honest answer: sometimes. Here's how to tell the difference between one that helps and one that's just expensive.</p>
        <span class="read-more">Read more →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="grade-nav">
    <a class="back" href="/timeline">← Back to the timeline</a>
    <a class="next" href="/grades/11">Next grade →</a>
  </nav>
</article>

<style>
:root{
  --paper:#FAF4EA;
  --ink:#12283D;
  --ink-soft:#4A5C70;
  --ink-faint:#7A8899;
  --rule:#E4D9C6;
  --g6:#E6F1FB;
  --g7:#B5D4F4;
  --g8:#85B7EB;
  --g9:#378ADD;
  --g10:#185FA5;
  --g11:#0C447C;
  --g12:#042C53;
}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{
  margin:0;
  background:var(--paper);
  color:var(--ink);
  font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif;
  font-size:16px;
  line-height:1.6;
  -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;
}
.grade-page{max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;padding:80px 24px 120px}
.grade-head{text-align:center;margin-bottom:56px}
.grade-badge{
  width:48px;height:48px;margin:0 auto 20px;border-radius:50%;
  background:var(--g10);border:1px solid var(--g11);color:#fff;
  display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:20px;
}
.eyebrow{display:block;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--g10);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.06em;margin-bottom:14px}
.grade-head h1{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:700;font-size:34px;line-height:1.2;margin:0 0 14px;letter-spacing:-0.01em;text-wrap:balance}
.lede{font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--ink-soft);margin:0}

.grade-section{margin-bottom:40px}
.grade-section h2{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:19px;color:var(--g10);margin:0 0 12px}
.grade-section p{font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--ink);margin:0 0 12px}
.grade-section p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
.grade-section ul{margin:0;padding-left:20px}
.grade-section li{font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--ink);margin-bottom:8px}
.grade-section li:last-child{margin-bottom:0}

.related{margin-bottom:40px}
.related h2{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:19px;color:var(--g10);margin:0 0 16px}
.related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));gap:16px}
.article-card{
  display:block;padding:24px;border-radius:14px;
  background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule);text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);
}
.article-card:hover{border-color:var(--g10)}
.article-card:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--g10);outline-offset:3px}
.article-card h3{font-family:Fraunces,serif;font-weight:600;font-size:18px;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 10px}
.article-card p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--ink-soft);margin:0 0 14px}
.article-card .read-more{font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--g10)}

.grade-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:8px}
.back{font-size:14px;color:var(--g10);text-decoration:none;font-weight:500}
.back:hover{text-decoration:underline}
.back:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--g10);outline-offset:3px}
.next{font-size:14px;color:var(--g10);text-decoration:none;font-weight:500}
.next:hover{text-decoration:underline}
.next:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--g10);outline-offset:3px}

@media (max-width:640px){
  .grade-page{padding:56px 20px 96px}
  .grade-head h1{font-size:28px}
}
</style>
</body>
</html>
